---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, href } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'October 12, 2026';
const toc = [
  ['ownership', 'Your work is yours'],
  ['acceptance', '1. Acceptance'],
  ['license', '2. Licence'],
  ['beta', '3. Beta software'],
  ['content', '4. Content you download and post'],
  ['platforms', '5. Third-party platforms'],
  ['agents', '6. Agents and automations'],
  ['backups', '7. Your data and backups'],
  ['warranty', '8. No warranty'],
  ['liability', '9. Limitation of liability'],
  ['changes', '10. Changes'],
  ['contact', '11. Contact'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Service: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Reelay Studio Terms of Service: the desktop software licence, your ownership of your work, the beta, content rights and third-party platform terms."
>
  <header class="doc-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede">The agreement for using the Reelay Studio desktop app and this website. <strong>Plain where we could make it plain.</strong></p>
      <p class="doc-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap doc-layout">
    <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <div>
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ol>{toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <section id="ownership" class="doc-summary">
        <h2>Your work is yours</h2>
        <p>Your videos, captions, transcripts, notes and everything else you make or keep in Reelay belong to you. Reelay claims no rights in them, and they stay on your computer.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="acceptance">
        <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
        <p>By downloading, installing or using the Reelay Studio desktop application (the “Software”) or using this website, you agree to these Terms. If you don’t agree, don’t install or use the Software.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="license">
        <h2>2. Licence</h2>
        <p>We grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and run the Software on computers you own or control, for your own content work or work you do for creators you manage. You may not resell or redistribute the Software, or remove its notices.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="beta">
        <h2>3. Beta software</h2>
        <p>Reelay {SITE.version} is a beta. It is free to use during the beta. Features may change, and some described on this site depend on approvals from third-party platforms that may change or be withdrawn. Pricing after the beta has not been set.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="content">
        <h2>4. Content you download and post</h2>
        <p>Reelay is built for content you own or have permission to use. You agree:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>to download and republish only videos, sounds and other material you own or are authorised to use;</li>
          <li>to record accurate permission and provenance details when you set them on a ticket;</li>
          <li>not to use the Software to infringe anyone’s copyright, trademark, privacy or other rights, or to break any law;</li>
          <li>not to use the Software to send spam or to get around a platform’s limits or safety systems.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="platforms">
        <h2>5. Third-party platforms</h2>
        <p>When you connect an account, your use of that platform through Reelay is also governed by its own terms, which you agree to follow:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>YouTube:</strong> the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Instagram, Facebook and Threads:</strong> Meta’s Terms of Service and the terms of each product.</li>
          <li><strong>TikTok:</strong> the TikTok Terms of Service.</li>
          <li><strong>Bluesky:</strong> the Bluesky Terms of Service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Reelay talks to these platforms on your behalf from your computer. We are not responsible for a platform’s decisions about your account, its rate limits, its review of an upload, or changes to its API.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="agents">
        <h2>6. Agents and automations</h2>
        <p>Reelay lets automations and AI agents you connect draft and change tickets, and lets agents request actions such as scheduling a post, which wait for a person’s approval. You are responsible for what you approve, for the rules you create, and for reviewing any text an AI tool suggests before it is published. If you connect an agent that uses a third-party AI service, that service’s terms apply to it.</p>
        <p>You agree not to bypass, or attempt to bypass, the approval step, the Ready gate or the access key that protect the Agent API.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="backups">
        <h2>7. Your data and backups</h2>
        <p>Because Reelay keeps your data on your computer and not on our servers, we cannot restore it for you. You are responsible for backing up your video files and Reelay’s database. How to find, move or delete that data is described in the <a href={href('/privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href={href('/data-deletion')}>User Data Deletion Instructions</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="warranty">
        <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
        <p>THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SOFTWARE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED OR ERROR-FREE, OR THAT ANY THIRD-PARTY PLATFORM WILL CONTINUE TO WORK WITH IT.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="liability">
        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, REELAY STUDIO AND ITS CONTRIBUTORS WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, USE OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE. Nothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms. We will change the date at the top when we do. If you keep using the Software after an update, the updated Terms apply.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Questions about these Terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.complianceEmail}`}>{SITE.complianceEmail}</a></li>
          <li>Help with the app: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
